                            <comment id="15236294" author="jeffsteinmetz" created="Tue, 12 Apr 2016 00:12:22 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This is a similar situation in R.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Perhaps all globally scoped variables in Python and R should start with&lt;br/&gt;
zeppelin_&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;or&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;_zeppelin (in R)&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15944146" author="vinayshukla@gmail.com" created="Mon, 27 Mar 2017 22:28:58 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I have also seen this issue when a user from scientific community defines a variable named Z and it conflicts with built in ZeppelinContext variable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Having a customizable name for Zeppelin context would be useful.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
